div.p:
Description:—Bulb  3 cm. in diameter, globose or ovoid, covered with pale brown papery tunics, and produced into a distinct neck up to 3·5 cm. long. Leaves  4-6, arising from a sheath, 2·2-4·5 cm. long, 1·2 cm. broad, oblanceolate or oblong (strap-shaped), rounded at the apex, glabrous. Leaf-
                  {32}
                  sheath  1·5-2 cm. in diameter, funnel-shaped, truncate, fleshy, reddish. Peduncle  lateral, 15-23 cm. long, terete, glabrous. Spathe-valves  reddish, 2-3·2 cm. long, longer or shorter than the pedicels. Pedicels  slender, 1·2-2 cm. long, glabrous. Inflorescence  13-25-flowered; flowers white, faintly but sweet-scented. Segments  1 cm. long, 3·6 mm. broad, lanceolate, obtuse. Filaments  connate into a tube for 5 mm., then free for 7 mm., erect, glabrous; anthers 2·5 mm. long, oblong, versatile. Ovary  1·5 mm. long, globose, glabrous, with about 5 ovules in each cell; style dilated, sharply 3-angled below and united with filaments; free part of style 5·5 mm. long, terete; stigma minutely 3-fid (National Herb., Pretoria, 2729).
